---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import EditorialSplit from '@components/sections/EditorialSplit.astro';
import SectionLabel from '@components/typography/SectionLabel.astro';
import Plate from '@components/media/Plate.astro';
import { mission, vision, positioning } from '@data/organisation';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Who We Are', href: '/who-we-are' },
  { label: 'Mission & Vision', href: '/who-we-are/mission' },
];

const IMG = '/images/who-we-are-mission-vision-page';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Mission & Vision"
  description="MMT Impact exists to strengthen communities and create sustainable opportunities through education, empowerment, social support, livelihoods and inclusive development."
  crumbs={crumbs}
  hero={{
    eyebrow: 'Who We Are / Mission & Vision',
    lines: ['What we exist', 'to do.'],
    lede: positioning,
    seed: 'mission-hero',
    src: `${IMG}/hero.jpg`,
    variant: 'horizon',
    size: 'compact',
  }}
>
  <!-- Mission — statement parallel to a portrait image -->
  <section class="stmt surface-paper section-sm" aria-labelledby="mission-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionLabel index="01" label="Mission" />
      <div class="stmt__grid">
        <p class="stmt__text" id="mission-h" data-reveal>{mission}</p>
        <div class="stmt__media" data-parallax-scope>
          <Plate
            seed="mission-statement"
            src={`${IMG}/01-mission.jpg`}
            variant="terrain"
            tone="navy"
            ratio="portrait"
            parallax={7}
            alt="Community members central to MMT Impact's mission, South Sudan"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Vision — reduced, fixed background photograph -->
  <section
    class="vstmt surface-dark"
    aria-labelledby="vision-h"
    style={`--vstmt-bg:url('${IMG}/02-vision.jpg')`}
  >
    <div class="vstmt__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap vstmt__inner">
      <SectionLabel index="02" label="Vision" />
      <p class="vstmt__text" id="vision-h" data-reveal>{vision}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EditorialSplit
    index="03"
    label="What this means"
    heading={'A mission is only\nuseful if it excludes\nsomething.'}
    ratio="lead"
    gap="tight"
    sticky
    size="sm"
    surface="light"
    id="meaning"
  >
    <Plate
      slot="lead"
      seed="mission-meaning"
      src={`${IMG}/03-What-this-means.jpg`}
      variant="cohort"
      tone="navy"
      ratio="wide"
      alt=""
    />

    <div class="prose-editorial">
      <p>
        Most organisational missions could be adopted by any organisation in the sector without
        changing a word. Ours is meant to be narrower than that, and the narrowing is deliberate.
      </p>

      <h3>Strengthen communities</h3>
      <p>
        Our unit of work is the community, not the individual beneficiary and not the national
        indicator. That determines how we assess need, who validates our targeting, and who we are
        accountable to first.
      </p>

      <h3>Create sustainable opportunities</h3>
      <p>
        An opportunity that exists only while a grant is running is not an opportunity, it is a
        stipend. We hold programmes to what remains once support ends — enterprises still trading,
        trainers still teaching, systems still operating.
      </p>

      <h3>Through education, empowerment, social support, livelihoods and inclusive development</h3>
      <p>
        These are our instruments. We do not present ourselves as a specialist health, nutrition,
        WASH or protection agency. Where a community need falls outside our competence, our
        obligation is a safe referral to an organisation mandated to meet it, not an extension of
        our own scope to capture the funding.
      </p>

      <h3>Inclusive</h3>
      <p>
        Inclusion is a design requirement rather than a reporting category. If a programme’s results
        cannot be disaggregated to show reach among women, young people, people with disabilities
        and displaced households, we treat that as a design failure, not a data limitation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </EditorialSplit>

  <EditorialSplit
    index="04"
    label="The vision, examined"
    heading={'A world where every\ncommunity has the\nopportunity to thrive.'}
    ratio="lead"
    gap="tight"
    sticky
    size="sm"
    surface="sand"
    id="vision-detail"
  >
    <Plate
      slot="lead"
      seed="mission-vision-detail"
      src={`${IMG}/04-The-vision-examined.jpg`}
      variant="horizon"
      tone="green"
      ratio="wide"
      alt=""
    />

    <div class="prose-editorial">
      <p>
        A vision statement describes an end state that the organisation will not, on its own, bring
        about. Ours is no exception, and stating it plainly matters more than the sentence itself.
      </p>
      <p>
        MMT Impact will not create a world where every community thrives. Governments, communities,
        markets and institutions will do that, or they will not. What an organisation of our kind
        can do is remove specific constraints in specific places — a training system that does not
        connect to employment, a producer group with no route to a buyer, a local organisation
        excluded from funding by a compliance gap — and do it well enough that the change holds.
      </p>
      <p>
        The word that carries the weight is <strong>opportunity</strong>. We are not in a position
        to guarantee outcomes for the people we work with, and we do not claim to be. We are in a
        position to widen the set of choices available to them, and to be measured on whether we
        did.
      </p>
    </div>
  </EditorialSplit>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  /* ---- 01 Mission: statement parallel to a portrait image ---- */
  .stmt__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .stmt__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 0.85fr);
    }
  }

  .stmt__text {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 4vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    max-width: 22ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .stmt__media {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  }

  .stmt__media :global(.frame),
  .stmt__media :global(.plate) {
    height: 100%;
  }

  /* ---- 02 Vision: reduced, fixed background photograph ----
     Same technique as the homepage focus band — a real `background-image`
     here instead of a generated plate, `background-attachment: fixed` only
     where a pointer device can render it smoothly. */
  .vstmt {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    background-image: var(--vstmt-bg);
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .vstmt {
      background-attachment: fixed;
    }
  }

  .vstmt__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(7 24 39 / 0.72), rgb(7 24 39 / 0.88));
  }

  .vstmt__text {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: #fff;
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

</style>
